  ($qb$HEAIL-ISF-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A2-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a newspaper stall. Six customers have mentioned a new magazine this week. You have space for one more title and three publishers are pushing theirs. How do you decide?$qb$, $qb$Find out whether the six would actually buy it every week$qb$, $qb$Count how often each title has been asked for$qb$, $qb$Ask the three publishers what the title sells elsewhere$qb$, $qb$Take the title the six mentioned$qb$, $qb$Take whichever publisher offers the best terms$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
