  ($qb$HEAIL-ISF-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A2-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a SIM card counter. Head office sends you six circulars a week and you have missed a price change that was in one of them. How do you handle it going forward?$qb$, $qb$Work out which circulars can change what you charge, and read those$qb$, $qb$Read every circular on the day it arrives$qb$, $qb$Ask head office to mark the important ones$qb$, $qb$Skim all six and file them$qb$, $qb$Wait for customers to point out any changes$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ISF-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A2-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a photocopy counter near a college. Students tell you about exam dates, syllabus changes and new courses. You need to plan paper stock. How do you use what you hear?$qb$, $qb$Track only what would change how much paper you order$qb$, $qb$Note everything students tell you and review it monthly$qb$, $qb$Ask the college office to confirm the dates$qb$, $qb$Order extra paper to cover all the possibilities$qb$, $qb$Order as you did last year, since patterns repeat$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
