  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-004$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$An idea nobody can explain in one sentence is hard to get anyone to ______.$qb$, $qb$back$qb$, $qb$write$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$email$qb$, $qb$file$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-005$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Combining two things that already work is often cheaper than inventing something ______.$qb$, $qb$new$qb$, $qb$cheap$qb$, $qb$quick$qb$, $qb$small$qb$, $qb$popular$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-006$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A rule that has never been questioned is a good place to look for a ______.$qb$, $qb$gap$qb$, $qb$cost$qb$, $qb$delay$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$warning$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The people who do a job every day hold ideas that nobody has ever ______ them about.$qb$, $qb$asked$qb$, $qb$paid$qb$, $qb$trained$qb$, $qb$praised$qb$, $qb$warned$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-008$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Judging ideas while you are still collecting them stops the ______ arriving.$qb$, $qb$unusual$qb$, $qb$obvious$qb$, $qb$cheapest$qb$, $qb$quickest$qb$, $qb$final$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-009$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A trial that costs a day tells you more than a discussion that lasts a ______.$qb$, $qb$month$qb$, $qb$lifetime$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, $qb$minute$qb$, $qb$season$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-010$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Copying an idea from a different trade works when the underlying problem is the ______.$qb$, $qb$same$qb$, $qb$smaller$qb$, $qb$older$qb$, $qb$cheaper$qb$, $qb$newer$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Removing a step is an idea as much as adding ______.$qb$, $qb$one$qb$, $qb$cost$qb$, $qb$time$qb$, $qb$detail$qb$, $qb$paperwork$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A proposal that only works if everyone behaves perfectly is not yet ______.$qb$, $qb$workable$qb$, $qb$expensive$qb$, $qb$written$qb$, $qb$popular$qb$, $qb$approved$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Writing down why an idea was rejected saves the next person ______ it.$qb$, $qb$reinventing$qb$, $qb$funding$qb$, $qb$explaining$qb$, $qb$shortening$qb$, $qb$approving$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The best time to try something unusual is when the cost of failing is ______.$qb$, $qb$low$qb$, $qb$shared$qb$, $qb$hidden$qb$, $qb$known$qb$, $qb$urgent$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Asking what would have to be true for an idea to work turns doubt into a ______.$qb$, $qb$test$qb$, $qb$delay$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$warning$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A change that helps you and costs another team is not an improvement but a ______.$qb$, $qb$transfer$qb$, $qb$saving$qb$, $qb$trial$qb$, $qb$shortcut$qb$, $qb$routine$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have an idea that would change how your team works. What is the best first step?$qb$, $qb$Try it on one small part and see what happens$qb$, $qb$Work out what it would cost to put in place$qb$, $qb$Explain it to the team and ask what they think$qb$, $qb$Take it to your manager for approval$qb$, $qb$Wait until you have thought it through fully$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A group is generating ideas and every suggestion is being debated as it arrives. What is the problem?$qb$, $qb$The unusual ideas stop being offered$qb$, $qb$The discussion takes longer than it needs to$qb$, $qb$The first ideas get more attention than the later ones$qb$, $qb$People argue instead of building on each other$qb$, $qb$The best idea may be missed in the noise$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want to improve something but have no budget. What is most useful to ask?$qb$, $qb$Which part of it could be changed for nothing$qb$, $qb$How much the improvement would cost$qb$, $qb$Whether the budget could be found elsewhere$qb$, $qb$Whether the improvement is worth funding$qb$, $qb$When the next budget becomes available$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your idea has been rejected and you think the reason given was wrong. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would have changed the decision$qb$, $qb$Explain why the reason does not apply$qb$, $qb$Ask for the decision to be looked at again$qb$, $qb$Try it on a small scale anyway$qb$, $qb$Accept it and move on to something else$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably tells you whether a new idea is worth adopting?$qb$, $qb$Trying it in a way that can be measured$qb$, $qb$Whether people who would use it support it$qb$, $qb$Whether it has worked somewhere similar$qb$, $qb$How much it would save if it worked$qb$, $qb$Whether it solves the problem in theory$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are stuck on a problem you have been working on for two days. What is most likely to help?$qb$, $qb$Describe it out loud to someone outside the work$qb$, $qb$Take a break and come back to it fresh$qb$, $qb$Look up how others have solved similar problems$qb$, $qb$Work through it more systematically$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague to take it over$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A process has six steps. Which question is most likely to lead to an improvement?$qb$, $qb$What would break if one step were removed$qb$, $qb$Which step takes the longest$qb$, $qb$Which step causes the most errors$qb$, $qb$Whether the steps are in the right order$qb$, $qb$Whether each step is necessary$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague has an idea you think will not work. What is the most useful response?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would have to be true for it to work$qb$, $qb$Explain why you think it will not work$qb$, $qb$Suggest testing it on something small$qb$, $qb$Ask others what they think of it$qb$, $qb$Let him try it and see what happens$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have three ideas and time to try one. How should you choose?$qb$, $qb$The one you could learn most from quickly$qb$, $qb$The one most likely to succeed$qb$, $qb$The one that would save the most if it worked$qb$, $qb$The one the team is most enthusiastic about$qb$, $qb$The one that is cheapest to try$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone in another trade solves a problem in a way that interests you. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Work out whether the underlying problem is the same$qb$, $qb$Try their method and see whether it transfers$qb$, $qb$Ask them how they arrived at the method$qb$, $qb$Adapt the method to fit your situation$qb$, $qb$Note it in case it becomes relevant$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually stops good ideas being raised in an organisation?$qb$, $qb$No clear route for an idea to reach a decision$qb$, $qb$People being too busy to think about them$qb$, $qb$Ideas being rejected without explanation$qb$, $qb$A lack of reward for raising them$qb$, $qb$Managers preferring things as they are$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have improved something and want it adopted more widely. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Show what changed, with the figures from your trial$qb$, $qb$Explain how the improvement works$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager to recommend it to others$qb$, $qb$Offer to help other teams put it in place$qb$, $qb$Write it up so others can read about it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$An idea worked well in one branch and failed in another. What is most useful to establish?$qb$, $qb$What was different about the two branches$qb$, $qb$Whether the second branch applied it properly$qb$, $qb$Whether the first branch's result was a fluke$qb$, $qb$Which branch is more typical of the business$qb$, $qb$Whether the idea needs adjusting before spreading$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to come up with ideas for reducing waste. What is the best starting point?$qb$, $qb$Watch where the waste actually happens$qb$, $qb$Ask the people doing the work what they see$qb$, $qb$Look at what the waste is costing$qb$, $qb$Find out how other places reduce it$qb$, $qb$List everything that could be cut$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new idea would help customers but make more work for your team. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out whether the extra work can be removed elsewhere$qb$, $qb$Weigh the benefit to customers against the cost$qb$, $qb$Ask the team whether the extra work is manageable$qb$, $qb$Try it and see how much extra work it really is$qb$, $qb$Drop it, since it makes the team's job harder$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been asked to make something faster. What question is most likely to help?$qb$, $qb$What the thing is actually for$qb$, $qb$Which part of it takes longest$qb$, $qb$Whether anyone has tried before$qb$, $qb$How much faster it needs to be$qb$, $qb$What tools could speed it up$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your trial of a new method produced mixed results. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Work out which parts worked and keep those$qb$, $qb$Run the trial again for longer$qb$, $qb$Ask the people involved what they thought$qb$, $qb$Drop it, since the results were not clear$qb$, $qb$Adopt it, since some of it worked$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to do with an idea you cannot act on now?$qb$, $qb$Write down the problem it would solve$qb$, $qb$Mention it to someone who might be able to use it$qb$, $qb$Write the idea out in full for your own records$qb$, $qb$Keep it in mind for when things change$qb$, $qb$Let it go, since ideas come round again$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two people have suggested opposite solutions to the same problem. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what each is assuming about the cause$qb$, $qb$Ask each to explain their reasoning$qb$, $qb$Try both on a small scale$qb$, $qb$Combine the parts of each that agree$qb$, $qb$Choose the one that is easier to try$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want your team to bring you more ideas. What is most likely to work?$qb$, $qb$Act visibly on the next one that arrives$qb$, $qb$Ask them regularly for suggestions$qb$, $qb$Set up a way for ideas to be submitted$qb$, $qb$Reward people who bring good ideas$qb$, $qb$Tell them ideas are welcome at any time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a small printing press. Customers regularly ask for jobs faster than your machines can produce them, and you lose about one order a week for this reason. Buying a faster machine is out of reach. How do you approach the problem?$qb$, $qb$Find out which parts of the job actually cause the wait, and test a change there$qb$, $qb$Look at where the delays happen across a week of orders$qb$, $qb$Ask customers how much faster they would need it to be$qb$, $qb$Ask staff whether they can work through the backlog faster$qb$, $qb$Accept the lost orders, since the machines are the limit$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a plant nursery. Half your stock of one popular plant dies each summer. Watering more has not helped. Staff have different theories. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Change one thing on a small block of plants and compare$qb$, $qb$Ask staff to record conditions on the plants that die$qb$, $qb$Ask a grower elsewhere how they keep the same plant alive$qb$, $qb$Try all the suggested changes across the whole stock$qb$, $qb$Order fewer of that plant, since it does not survive here$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a community radio station. Listener numbers have been flat for a year. Your team has plenty of programme ideas but no way of knowing which would work. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Run two of the ideas as one-off shows and compare response$qb$, $qb$Ask listeners which of the ideas they would tune in for$qb$, $qb$Look at what similar stations have added recently$qb$, $qb$Choose the idea the team is most enthusiastic about$qb$, $qb$Keep the schedule as it is, since listeners have not complained$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You own a furniture workshop. Offcuts of good timber are thrown away every week. A member of staff has suggested making small items from them. You are not sure they would sell. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Make a few and put them out for sale to find out$qb$, $qb$Ask her what she thinks could be made from them$qb$, $qb$Work out what the offcuts are currently costing you$qb$, $qb$Ask customers whether they would buy such items$qb$, $qb$Keep disposing of them, since the workshop makes furniture$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a swimming pool. Attendance drops sharply between two and four in the afternoon. The pool is staffed and heated throughout. How do you approach this?$qb$, $qb$Try one different use of those hours for a month and measure it$qb$, $qb$Find out who is nearby and free at that time of day$qb$, $qb$Ask regular users why they do not come then$qb$, $qb$Reduce the staffing during those hours$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since afternoons are quiet everywhere$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a taxi firm. Drivers spend a lot of time waiting at the airport for fares. One driver has suggested an arrangement with a nearby hotel. Nobody has tested it. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Agree a trial with the hotel and run it with two drivers for a fortnight$qb$, $qb$Ask him to explain how the arrangement would work in practice$qb$, $qb$Ask drivers at other firms whether such arrangements work$qb$, $qb$Ask the other drivers whether they would use such an arrangement$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the airport work is reliable enough$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a photo studio. School portrait season is your busiest period and you turn work away every year. Hiring seasonal staff has not worked well. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Look at which part of the job everything else waits on$qb$, $qb$Work out how much work you turn away each season$qb$, $qb$Try a different approach to seasonal hiring$qb$, $qb$Ask schools to book earlier so the work is spread$qb$, $qb$Accept the limit, since the season is short$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a cycle shop. Repairs take three days because parts arrive slowly. A customer has suggested you stock the ten most common parts. You have limited space. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Check which parts you have ordered most often this year$qb$, $qb$Work out what stocking those parts would cost$qb$, $qb$Ask your supplier whether delivery could be faster$qb$, $qb$Stock the parts and see whether repairs speed up$qb$, $qb$Explain to customers that parts take time to arrive$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a food truck. Sales are strong at lunchtime and poor in the evening. Your menu is the same all day. How do you approach the evening problem?$qb$, $qb$Try a different evening offer for two weeks and compare takings$qb$, $qb$Find out who is around in the evening and what they want$qb$, $qb$Ask lunchtime customers whether they would come in the evening$qb$, $qb$Move to a different location for the evenings$qb$, $qb$Stop trading in the evening and save the cost$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a dairy. A member of staff has suggested a change to the bottling line that he says would save time. He has no figures and you cannot spare the line for a trial. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Time the current step so there is a figure to compare against$qb$, $qb$Ask him to explain in detail how the change would work$qb$, $qb$Ask the line manufacturer whether the change is possible$qb$, $qb$Try it during a scheduled maintenance window$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the line cannot be stopped for trials$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a driving school. Learners often cancel at short notice and the slots go unfilled. You have tried charging for late cancellation and it made customers unhappy. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Find out what makes learners cancel late, then test one change$qb$, $qb$Look at when the cancellations mostly happen$qb$, $qb$Keep a list of learners who would take a slot at short notice$qb$, $qb$Overbook slightly to allow for cancellations$qb$, $qb$Accept the cancellations as part of the business$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a museum. Visitors spend an average of eighteen minutes in a gallery that took a year to build. You expected much longer. How do you approach this?$qb$, $qb$Watch where visitors stop and where they walk past$qb$, $qb$Ask visitors on the way out what they saw$qb$, $qb$Compare the layout with a gallery that holds people longer$qb$, $qb$Add more information panels to give people more to read$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since eighteen minutes may be normal$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a catering firm. Clients keep asking for a service you do not offer, and you have turned down eleven enquiries this year. Setting it up properly would cost a lot. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Take one booking and deliver it in the simplest way possible$qb$, $qb$Work out what setting the service up would actually cost$qb$, $qb$Ask the eleven clients what exactly they wanted$qb$, $qb$Refer the enquiries to another firm for a fee$qb$, $qb$Keep declining them and focus on your existing work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-INV-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A2-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a hostel. Guests complain that the kitchen is crowded between seven and eight in the evening. The kitchen cannot be enlarged. How do you approach the problem?$qb$, $qb$Try one change to how the hour is used and see whether it helps$qb$, $qb$Watch what guests are actually doing in that hour$qb$, $qb$Ask guests what would make the kitchen easier to use$qb$, $qb$Put up a notice asking guests to spread their cooking times$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since the kitchen is the size it is$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-001$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Speeding up one step in a chain only helps if that step was the ______ one.$qb$, $qb$slowest$qb$, $qb$first$qb$, $qb$cheapest$qb$, $qb$newest$qb$, $qb$busiest$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-002$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A queue forms wherever work arrives faster than it can be ______.$qb$, $qb$cleared$qb$, $qb$counted$qb$, $qb$measured$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, $qb$approved$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-003$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Fixing a problem in one department often moves it to ______.$qb$, $qb$another$qb$, $qb$nobody$qb$, $qb$everyone$qb$, $qb$later$qb$, $qb$history$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-004$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A process is only as reliable as the step with the most ______.$qb$, $qb$variation$qb$, $qb$staff$qb$, $qb$cost$qb$, $qb$history$qb$, $qb$documentation$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-005$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Adding a check without removing a cause increases the work and not the ______.$qb$, $qb$quality$qb$, $qb$cost$qb$, $qb$margin$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$process$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-006$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Two teams each meeting their own target can still miss the ______ one.$qb$, $qb$shared$qb$, $qb$monthly$qb$, $qb$written$qb$, $qb$annual$qb$, $qb$local$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Time spent waiting between steps never shows up in any step's own ______.$qb$, $qb$figures$qb$, $qb$staffing$qb$, $qb$training$qb$, $qb$premises$qb$, $qb$equipment$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-008$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A rule introduced to stop one rare event is paid for by every ______ case.$qb$, $qb$ordinary$qb$, $qb$future$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, $qb$past$qb$, $qb$similar$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-009$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$If a fault only appears when two things happen together, testing them separately proves ______.$qb$, $qb$nothing$qb$, $qb$everything$qb$, $qb$half$qb$, $qb$much$qb$, $qb$both$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-010$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The output of a process cannot be more consistent than its ______.$qb$, $qb$inputs$qb$, $qb$staff$qb$, $qb$targets$qb$, $qb$records$qb$, $qb$premise$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Measuring one part of a system encourages people to improve that part at the expense of the ______.$qb$, $qb$rest$qb$, $qb$target$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$budget$qb$, $qb$customer$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A delay early in a chain is cheaper to absorb than the same delay at the ______.$qb$, $qb$end$qb$, $qb$start$qb$, $qb$review$qb$, $qb$office$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$When everyone follows the rules and the result is still poor, the fault is in the ______.$qb$, $qb$design$qb$, $qb$staff$qb$, $qb$training$qb$, $qb$effort$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Batching work makes each batch efficient and every individual item ______.$qb$, $qb$slower$qb$, $qb$cheaper$qb$, $qb$safer$qb$, $qb$smaller$qb$, $qb$clearer$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A system with no spare capacity turns every small problem into a ______.$qb$, $qb$delay$qb$, $qb$cost$qb$, $qb$complaint$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$qualification$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Understanding where work comes from tells you more than watching what you ______.$qb$, $qb$receive$qb$, $qb$send$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$count$qb$, $qb$approve$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A queue has formed at one point in a five-step process. What is most useful to establish?$qb$, $qb$Whether work is arriving faster than that step can clear it$qb$, $qb$Whether that step is being done too slowly$qb$, $qb$Whether that step needs more people$qb$, $qb$How long the queue has been building$qb$, $qb$What the queue is costing in delay$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your department has improved its own figures and the overall result has not moved. What is most likely?$qb$, $qb$The gain has been absorbed elsewhere in the chain$qb$, $qb$The overall measure is not sensitive enough$qb$, $qb$The improvement was too small to show$qb$, $qb$Other departments have got worse$qb$, $qb$The figures are being calculated differently$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A fault appears about once a month and never when anyone is watching. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Record the conditions each time it happens$qb$, $qb$Watch the process more closely$qb$, $qb$Ask the operators what they notice$qb$, $qb$Replace the part most likely to be failing$qb$, $qb$Wait until it happens while someone is present$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when a new check is added to a process?$qb$, $qb$The work grows and the cause stays where it was$qb$, $qb$Errors are caught earlier than before$qb$, $qb$The process becomes slower but safer$qb$, $qb$People find ways around the check$qb$, $qb$The number of recorded errors rises$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two teams both hit their targets and the customer is still unhappy. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what happens between the two teams$qb$, $qb$Ask the customer what is going wrong$qb$, $qb$Check whether the targets measure the right things$qb$, $qb$Look at each team's work more closely$qb$, $qb$Combine the two targets into one$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to speed up a process. What should you establish first?$qb$, $qb$Where the work spends time without being worked on$qb$, $qb$Which step takes the longest$qb$, $qb$Which step has the most people$qb$, $qb$How long the whole process takes now$qb$, $qb$What the target time is$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A problem was fixed in your area and has appeared in the next area along. What does this suggest?$qb$, $qb$The problem was moved rather than removed$qb$, $qb$The next area has a similar weakness$qb$, $qb$The fix was not applied thoroughly enough$qb$, $qb$The two areas share a common cause$qb$, $qb$The problem has spread from your area$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to know about a process you have inherited?$qb$, $qb$Which steps exist because something once went wrong$qb$, $qb$How long each step takes$qb$, $qb$Who is responsible for each step$qb$, $qb$Where the errors usually occur$qb$, $qb$How often the process runs$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A step in your process is often skipped when things are busy. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what the step catches when it is done$qb$, $qb$Make the step quicker to complete$qb$, $qb$Check that the step is being done$qb$, $qb$Remind people the step is required$qb$, $qb$Move the step to a quieter point in the day$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Output is inconsistent although everyone follows the same method. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Look at what varies in what arrives at the process$qb$, $qb$Watch several people carrying out the method$qb$, $qb$Check whether the method is written clearly$qb$, $qb$Compare the output of different operators$qb$, $qb$Retrain everyone on the method$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your process has spare capacity on three steps and none on the fourth. What follows?$qb$, $qb$The fourth step sets the pace for everything$qb$, $qb$The three steps are overstaffed$qb$, $qb$The fourth step needs more resources$qb$, $qb$The process is unbalanced$qb$, $qb$Work will accumulate before the fourth step$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful measure of how well a process is working?$qb$, $qb$How long work takes from arriving to leaving$qb$, $qb$How much each step produces$qb$, $qb$How many errors are found$qb$, $qb$How busy the people are$qb$, $qb$How much it costs to run$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A change improved things for a month and then results returned to where they were. What is most likely?$qb$, $qb$The old way reasserted itself once attention moved on$qb$, $qb$The change was not a real improvement$qb$, $qb$Conditions changed after the first month$qb$, $qb$People stopped following the new method$qb$, $qb$The measurement was affected by the attention$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are told a step cannot be removed because of a regulation. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what the regulation actually requires$qb$, $qb$Ask who introduced the step originally$qb$, $qb$Look for a quicker way to do the step$qb$, $qb$Accept it and look elsewhere for savings$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the regulation still applies$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Work is batched into weekly runs for efficiency. What does this cost?$qb$, $qb$Each item waits up to a week before it moves$qb$, $qb$Errors are found a week after they are made$qb$, $qb$The process cannot respond to urgent work$qb$, $qb$Capacity is idle between the runs$qb$, $qb$Nothing, since batching is more efficient$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably tells you where a process is failing?$qb$, $qb$Following one piece of work all the way through$qb$, $qb$Asking the people who work in it$qb$, $qb$Looking at where errors are recorded$qb$, $qb$Timing each of the steps$qb$, $qb$Comparing it with a similar process elsewhere$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two problems always occur together. What is most useful to establish?$qb$, $qb$Whether one causes the other or both share a cause$qb$, $qb$Which of the two happens first$qb$, $qb$How often each occurs without the other$qb$, $qb$The cost of each one when it happens on its own$qb$, $qb$Whether anyone has noticed the pattern before$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A process works well at normal volume and fails at peak. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find which step runs out of capacity first$qb$, $qb$Add people across the process at peak$qb$, $qb$Spread the peak volume across more time$qb$, $qb$Find out how much above normal the peak is$qb$, $qb$Accept that peaks cause problems$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have improved a step and the people after it are now busier. What does this mean?$qb$, $qb$You have moved the constraint, not removed it$qb$, $qb$The next step now needs looking at$qb$, $qb$The improvement is working as intended$qb$, $qb$More work is getting through overall$qb$, $qb$The process is better balanced than before$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful question to ask about a form that everyone complains about?$qb$, $qb$What is done with each field after it is filled in$qb$, $qb$Which fields people find hardest$qb$, $qb$How long the form takes to complete$qb$, $qb$Who designed the form originally$qb$, $qb$Whether the form could be shortened$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a hospital laundry. Wards complain that linen arrives late, but your machines run at full capacity all day and your output matches demand. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Follow one trolley from ward to ward and see where the time goes$qb$, $qb$Ask the wards when they need linen and when it arrives$qb$, $qb$Compare your output figures against ward complaints$qb$, $qb$Add an extra delivery run to the wards each day$qb$, $qb$Explain to the wards that the laundry is at full capacity$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a seed certification office. Farmers complain the certificate takes three weeks. Each of your four stages takes under a day of actual work. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Find out where the file sits between the four stages$qb$, $qb$Time each of the four stages accurately$qb$, $qb$Ask the staff at each stage what slows them$qb$, $qb$Add a fifth person to speed the stages up$qb$, $qb$Tell farmers three weeks is normal for certification$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a toll plaza. One lane is always congested while the others flow freely. The lanes have identical equipment and staffing. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Watch what arrives in that lane and how drivers choose lanes$qb$, $qb$Move the operator from that lane to another$qb$, $qb$Ask the operator in that lane what happens$qb$, $qb$Open an extra lane during the congested periods$qb$, $qb$Direct traffic away from the congested lane$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a paper recycling depot. Your sorting line meets its daily target but the baling press is idle half the day and running late into the evening. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Match the sorting output to the press across the day$qb$, $qb$Ask the press operator why the work arrives unevenly$qb$, $qb$Extend the press operator's hours to cover the evening$qb$, $qb$Increase the sorting target so the press stays busy$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the sorting target is being met$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise bus ticket printing. Depots order in bulk once a month and you have a large rush in the last week. The presses are idle in the first two weeks. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Agree staggered ordering dates with the depots$qb$, $qb$Ask the depots why they all order at month end$qb$, $qb$Take on extra staff for the last week$qb$, $qb$Print stock in advance during the quiet weeks$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since monthly ordering is the depots' choice$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a cattle market. Weighing takes four minutes per animal and the pens hold sixty. Sellers arrive across two hours and complain about the wait. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Work out what sixty animals at four minutes needs, then set arrival slots$qb$, $qb$Add a second weighing station for busy periods$qb$, $qb$Ask sellers to arrive earlier in the morning$qb$, $qb$Speed up the weighing to under four minutes$qb$, $qb$Explain to sellers that weighing takes time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run an ice cream cold chain. Product arrives at retailers soft about once a fortnight, always from different vans and different routes. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Find what those deliveries have in common besides the vans$qb$, $qb$Check the refrigeration on each van in turn$qb$, $qb$Ask the drivers what happens on those days$qb$, $qb$Fit temperature recorders to all the vans$qb$, $qb$Instruct drivers to reduce their delivery times$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a municipal water testing lab. Samples are tested within a day but results reach the public health office a week later. Your lab is not the delay. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Trace what happens to a result after it leaves your lab$qb$, $qb$Send results directly to the public health office$qb$, $qb$Ask the public health office when they receive them$qb$, $qb$Speed up your own testing further$qb$, $qb$Report that your lab is testing within a day$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a ration shop. Queues are long on the first three days of the month and the shop is empty for the rest. Your stock and staffing are the same all month. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Find out what makes people come in the first three days$qb$, $qb$Add staff for the first three days of each month$qb$, $qb$Ask people to spread their visits across the month$qb$, $qb$Open longer hours during the busy days$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since ration collection is always month-start$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run examination board despatch. Papers reach schools on time but answer scripts come back late from a third of schools every session. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Find out what is different about that third of schools$qb$, $qb$Send reminders to schools about the return date$qb$, $qb$Ask the late schools why the scripts are delayed$qb$, $qb$Arrange collection from schools rather than return by post$qb$, $qb$Build the late returns into your marking timetable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a plywood press shop. Output is good but about one sheet in twenty comes out with uneven glue. It happens across all three presses and all shifts. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Look at what all three presses share, such as the glue supply$qb$, $qb$Check each press for pressure and temperature faults$qb$, $qb$Ask the operators when the uneven sheets appear$qb$, $qb$Increase the pressing time on all three presses$qb$, $qb$Sort the uneven sheets out at the end of the line$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a courier last-mile hub. Your sorters finish by nine and the vans leave at eleven. The two hours are spent waiting for the long-distance trunk vehicle. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Take the arrival time of the trunk vehicle to whoever schedules it$qb$, $qb$Find out why the trunk vehicle arrives when it does$qb$, $qb$Load the vans with what has arrived and send a second run$qb$, $qb$Ask the sorters to start later so they finish nearer eleven$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since the trunk vehicle is outside your control$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage pathology sample transport between four clinics and one lab. Samples from one clinic are regularly rejected as too old. That clinic is nearest the lab. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Look at when samples are collected there, not how far they travel$qb$, $qb$Increase the number of collections from that clinic$qb$, $qb$Ask the clinic staff when they take the samples$qb$, $qb$Ask the lab to be less strict with that clinic's samples$qb$, $qb$Move that clinic to the start of the collection round$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SPT-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A2-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a grain procurement centre. Farmers wait hours to unload, but your unloading bays are empty for long stretches. Weighing, testing and payment happen in sequence. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Find out which of the three stages the queue is actually waiting for$qb$, $qb$Add a second unloading bay to increase capacity$qb$, $qb$Ask farmers to arrive at staggered times$qb$, $qb$Speed up the weighing, which is the first stage$qb$, $qb$Extend the centre's opening hours$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
